     "label": "PREDICTED VARIATION",
     "question": "How many of the four rows of p -> q and q -> p differ?",
     "answer": "Two rows: (p, q) = (true, false) and (false, true)",
     "why": "Both are true at (true, true) and (false, false) and both are false in the swapped rows. Two differing rows is exactly why the converse is not equivalent."
