    "work": "f'(x) = 3x^2 + 2, and 3x^2 >= 0, so f'(x) >= 2 > 0 everywhere. Take any x1 < x2; the mean value theorem on [x1, x2] gives f(x2) - f(x1) = f'(c)(x2 - x1) with f'(c) > 0 and x2 - x1 > 0.",
