     "answer": "(C) 0.5 and 1.",
     "why": "F(-1) = P(X <= -1) = 0.5 includes the mass at -1 itself; F(1) = P(X <= 1) = 1 adds the mass at +1. Option (A) comes from using < instead of <=, which is the whole point of the question."
